    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this does not show",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 49
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "- **Zero is not proof of readiness.** It only means no plaintext caller was seen in the range; Jobs, backups, failover paths and rare admin clients may not have run. Use this as one input to the STRICT decision, not a pass/fail gate.\n- **Same-node host-network callers are invisible.** Kubelet probes, the Gateway's envoy and any `hostNetwork` pod on the workload's node bypass ztunnel, so they appear in neither metric, and `STRICT` does not apply to them either. Callers that only show up cross-node still break when pods move; check the existing Cilium policy and ztunnel access logs too.\n- **Only enrolled destinations report.** Traffic to unenrolled namespaces is not counted.\n- **Pre-enrollment connections stay outside the mesh** until the workload restarts, so restart after enrolling before reading this.\n- Counts come from 60 s scrapes; ranges shorter than ~5 minutes are noisy. See README \"Istio Ambient\"."
      },
